# Pinned trusted signers for machine-evidence attestations (OpenSSH allowed_signers format).
#
# These public keys verify signed MCP-client evidence and CI run-provenance.
# They provide artifact integrity; they do NOT define Arvyx release governance.
# Release governance is documented multi-model review under
# `.arvyx/model-reviews/` and `.arvyx/release-reviews/`.
#
# Empty/comment-only means signed machine evidence cannot verify (fail closed).
# Never store a private key in this repository.
#
# Being pinned is not the same as being release-grade. Pinning decides whether a
# signature verifies; `docs/release-grade-signers.allowed` decides whose signature
# can carry a *public* release. `arvyx release-candidate` blocks the public
# verdict when supplied provenance or MCP evidence is signed by a pinned principal
# that is absent from that list, so a host-drill signature cannot open the public
# gate even though it verifies. A missing or comment-only list blocks the public
# verdict rather than falling back to any pinned signer.
#
# Format (one signer per line):
#   <principal> <keytype> <base64-public-key>
# Example:
#   ci-release@example ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...REPLACE_ME
#
# MCP evidence signing:
#   arvyx evidence sign --evidence <file.json> --key <ssh_private_key> --principal <pinned-id>
# CI provenance signing:
#   arvyx attest provenance --check <id> --result pass --key <ssh_private_key> --principal <pinned-id> --output <file>

# CI release signer. The private key exists only as the `release-provenance`
# environment secret ARVEN_RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY; it is never written to disk in
# this repository or on the operator host. Provenance signed by this principal is
# the release-grade machine evidence.
# Rotation history is kept in the maintainers' decision records.
# Rotated 2026-11-02 for the public candidate pipeline (the previous key had no
# recoverable private half; no evidence was ever signed with it).
arven-release-tooling-ci ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIEHT3nXFEquantSksEqnDPIVYBg5CSuSjidU+2k3d6FW

# Production release signer. Pinned so its historical evidence keeps verifying.
arvyx-release-tooling ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAID7M7rxDzSU8KZCWYXmztEboSrH2owd59x0hG+5Ap8Rk
# Host drill signer. It is NOT release-grade: it can sign evidence that no CI run
# produced, so it must not satisfy a public-release gate. Kept pinned because the
# host drill and readiness flow signs with it; scoped by
# docs/release-grade-signers.allowed rather than silently trusted.
arven-release-tooling-local ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAebiogx/mBAGR74SvOldLPUyAfPsbv3laLEwAdsh4Kn
